WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:06.707
The next evening Daisy and her dad went outside.

2
00:00:06.708 --> 00:00:10.590
Kaleem was waiting in their backyard. "I brought a flashlight."

3
00:00:10.591 --> 00:00:15.582
"Thanks," Daisy said. "Dad's going to light the firepit for us."

4
00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:24.374
Beatrice buzzed over. "Did you decide on an animal, Daisy?"

5
00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:27.017
"Not yet," Daisy whispered back.

6
00:00:27.018 --> 00:00:32.545
"But I'll figure something out—I promise!"

7
00:00:32.546 --> 00:00:37.416
Daisy's dad lit the fire. "There you go, kids.

8
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:41.335
It should help to keep the bugs away.

9
00:00:41.336 --> 00:00:44.796
They're pretty bad this year."

10
00:00:44.797 --> 00:00:49.374
"Yeah." Kaleem waved away a few flying insects.

11
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:52.457
"I have like ten mosquito bites already!"

12
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:58.213
Daisy's dad chuckled. "I'll come back soon to check on you.

13
00:00:58.214 --> 00:01:00.291
Good luck with your bat watching."

14
00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:07.582
"Thanks," Daisy and Kaleem said.

15
00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:11.003
They sat down in lawn chairs by the fire.

16
00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:14.624
Beatrice settled onto the arm of Daisy's chair.

17
00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:19.137
Daisy told Kaleem what her parents had said about the disappearing bats.

18
00:01:19.138 --> 00:01:24.004
Kaleem's eyes went wide. "My parents said the same thing.

19
00:01:24.005 --> 00:01:26.497
What do you think happened to all the bats?"

20
00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:31.761
Daisy shrugged. "It's a mystery. But I think we can solve it.

21
00:01:31.762 --> 00:01:36.180
We just need to collect some clues."

22
00:01:36.181 --> 00:01:40.251
She spotted a mouse creeping past, heading for the woods.

23
00:01:40.252 --> 00:01:43.653
"Excuse me, mouse!" Daisy leaped up.

24
00:01:43.654 --> 00:01:48.866
"I have an important question. Have you seen any bats lately?"

25
00:01:48.867 --> 00:01:53.246
The mouse moved closer, keeping a wary eye on the fire.

26
00:01:53.247 --> 00:01:59.957
"No, but I mostly watch the sky for owls. They like to eat mice."

27
00:01:59.958 --> 00:02:03.125
The mouse scurried away as Daisy filled in Kaleem.

28
00:02:03.126 --> 00:02:09.311
A moment later an owl swooped low.

29
00:02:09.312 --> 00:02:13.956
"Yikes! Good thing that mouse got out of here," Kaleem said.

30
00:02:13.957 --> 00:02:20.280
Daisy nodded. Then she called to the owl and asked him about bats.

31
00:02:20.281 --> 00:02:24.993
The owl looked thoughtful. "I've seen a few recently."

32
00:02:24.994 --> 00:02:31.151
"You have?" Daisy said. She quickly told Kaleem the news. "Where?"

33
00:02:31.152 --> 00:02:34.750
"Deep in the forest," the owl said.

34
00:02:34.751 --> 00:02:41.454
"I don't think they come out this way much."

35
00:02:41.455 --> 00:02:46.279
"That's interesting," Daisy said after the owl flew off.

36
00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:49.416
Kaleem nodded, looking thoughtful.

37
00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:56.166
"Yet our parents remember seeing bats flying around our yards before. So what changed?"

38
00:02:56.167 --> 00:03:01.043
Daisy jumped up, distracted by a few tiny flashes of light.

39
00:03:01.044 --> 00:03:06.258
"Look, Kaleem, fireflies!

40
00:03:06.259 --> 00:03:09.607
That's the first time I've seen any this spring."

41
00:03:09.608 --> 00:03:13.240
Kaleem smiled. "I love seeing them!

42
00:03:13.241 --> 00:03:16.220
Remember when I went to visit my cousins last summer?"

43
00:03:16.221 --> 00:03:21.102
"Yes," Daisy said. "They live on a big farm, right?"

44
00:03:21.103 --> 00:03:23.258
"Right," Kaleem said.

45
00:03:23.259 --> 00:03:28.124
"They have tons of fireflies there. We caught some in a jar."

46
00:03:28.125 --> 00:03:34.442
Beatrice buzzed loudly with alarm. "You did what?"

47
00:03:34.443 --> 00:03:37.999
Daisy laughed and told Kaleem what Beatrice had said.

48
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.738
"Don't worry, Beatrice," Kaleem said.

49
00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:42.999
"We let them go after a few minutes.

50
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.499
But it was cool to see them light up in the jar.

51
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.406
It was like having a living flashlight!"

52
00:03:48.407 --> 00:03:53.020
Daisy watched the fireflies glowing dimly in her backyard.

53
00:03:53.021 --> 00:03:56.832
Then she glanced around at the houses surrounding hers.

54
00:03:56.833 --> 00:04:01.001
Light shone through the windows from interior rooms.

55
00:04:01.002 --> 00:04:06.196
It also shone from streetlamps and lights on porches and decks.

56
00:04:06.197 --> 00:04:10.374
Yet her backyard was a little darker than usual.

57
00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:13.434
"Kaleem, I've got it!" Daisy cried.

58
00:04:13.435 --> 00:04:19.418
"I just solved the missing bat mystery!"

